  "id": "prenatal-influence",
  "term": "prenatal influence",
  "definition": "Prenatal influence is an effect on offspring development that arises before birth, during fetal life. In this source, it refers to the possibility that differences between offspring are shaped not only by maternal care after birth but also by conditions in the womb, such as differences in fetal hormone exposure.",
